    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nRarely does a property come to market in Broadford that offers quite as much as No. 2 Broadford Avenue. Occupying a particularly generous corner site, this impressive five-bedroom semi-detached residence is a home of genuine distinction in an established and highly regarded residential setting. With the majority of properties in Broadford being traditional three-bedroom semi-detached homes, the scale and versatility of accommodation offered here makes this a particularly special opportunity.\n\nThe property is further enhanced by its unusually large gardens to the front, side and rear, providing excellent outdoor space and offering potential for further development, subject to the necessary planning permission. To the rear is a wonderful west-facing garden, ideal for enjoying the afternoon and evening sunshine, while the elevated position also affords a splendid outlook towards the Dublin Mountains.\nInternally, the property offers well-proportioned and exceptionally versatile accommodation extending to five bedrooms, two reception rooms and a superb open-plan kitchen, dining and sitting area spanning the width of the house. The accommodation is ideally suited to modern family living, with generous living and entertaining space on the ground floor and five bedrooms upstairs.\n\nBroadford is exceptionally well positioned, with a wealth of amenities close by and excellent access to Dundrum, the city centre and surrounding areas. There is an excellent choice of primary and secondary schools within easy reach, together with extensive recreational facilities and green spaces nearby. The location, combined with the scale, gardens and potential of the property, makes this a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial family home in this much sought-after location."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 4.65m x 4.80m\nWelcoming entrance hall with wood-effect flooring and staircase rising to the first floor. Door to guest WC.\n\nGuest Bathroom - 1.60m x 0.85m\nWash hand basin with vanity/storage cupboard beneath and WC.\n\nLiving Room - 4.10m x 3.90m\nA bright and well-proportioned reception room with large picture window overlooking the front garden. Wood-effect flooring and open fireplace with brass inset and slate hearth. Double doors open through to the kitchen/dining/sitting area.\n\nFamily Room - 4.75m x 3.45m\nSeparate reception room with window overlooking the front garden.\n\nKitchen/Dining/Sitting Area - 3.65m x 5.80m\nA magnificent room spanning the full width of the property, incorporating generous dining and informal sitting areas. The room enjoys excellent natural light with a window overlooking the rear garden, a wood-burning stove and double doors opening directly onto the rear garden. Wood-effect flooring throughout.Kitchen: Traditional-style hand-painted kitchen with an excellent range of wall-mounted units, drawers and cupboards, built-in Bosch oven, Electrolux hob and extractor, plumbing for washing machine and dishwasher, part-tiled walls and tiled floor.\n\nFirst Floor Landing - 3.19m x 3.25m\nLarge landing with access to attic, together with hot press/airing cupboard.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.85m x 3.70m\nExcellent double bedroom positioned to the front with window overlooking the front garden.\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.35m x 3.20m\nDouble bedroom to the rear with built-in wardrobes and overhead storage cupboards.\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.60m x 2.60m\nGood-sized single bedroom to the rear.\n\nBedroom 4 - 2.60m x 3.45m\nGenerous double bedroom to the rear with window overlooking the garden.\n\nBedroom 5 - 2.70mx 3.45m\nSingle bedroom to the front with window overlooking the terrace area and front garden.\n\nFamily Bathroom - 2.10m x 2.00m\nFully tiled bathroom with bath incorporating Triton T90SR electric shower, wash hand basin with vanity/storage unit beneath, WC and heated towel rail.\n\nOutside - \nThis exceptional property occupies a generous corner site with gardens extending to the front, side and rear. The front garden provides substantial off-street parking together with a lawned area, mature tree and established hedgerow, while pedestrian access to the side leads through to the rear garden. The rear garden is predominantly laid in level lawn and is bordered by mature planting and hedging, creating a private and attractive outdoor space. A substantial concrete-built shed provides useful additional storage and houses the oil-fired central heating boiler. The generous side garden and overall site provide excellent scope for future enhancement, subject to the necessary planning permission. A particular feature is the west-facing rear garden, while the position of the property also enjoys a wonderful outlook towards the Dublin Mountains.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Exceptional five-bedroom semi-detached family home</li><li>Particularly generous corner site with extensive gardens</li><li>Wonderful west-facing rear garden</li><li>Potential for further development, subject to planning permission</li><li>Superb kitchen, dining and sitting area spanning the width of the property</li><li>Two excellent reception rooms</li><li>Generous off-street parking for several vehicles</li><li>Double-glazed windows and oil-fired central heating</li><li>Approx. 140 sq. m. / 1506 sq. ft.</ul>"
      },
